# Runtime + secrets for the soc-recon bundle — never commit these.
#
# INLINE `#` COMMENTS DO NOT WORK IN .gitignore. A trailing comment becomes part
# of the pattern, so the line matches a filename that does not exist and ignores
# nothing — silently. This file had three such lines from 2026-06-20 until
# 2026-08-09; `data/`, `scope/domains.txt` and the cert dir were all live in a
# public repo the whole time. (The same trap was already logged once, on
# 2026-07-11, against the ROOT .gitignore — it just was not checked here.)
# No key material was ever exposed: the root .gitignore's `*.pem` / `*.key`
# extension rules caught every cert and private key independently. The real gap
# was the recon scope + run outputs.
# Verify changes here with `git check-ignore -v <path>`, never by eye.
.env
# recon run outputs + triage working dir (host-visible volume)
data/
# live scope; only domains.txt.example is tracked
scope/domains.txt
# generated TLS certs + private keys — never commit
config/wazuh_indexer_ssl_certs/
# Holds real bcrypt password hashes once rotated off the Wazuh demo defaults.
# Publishing password hashes to a public portfolio repo is exactly what ISA
# "no real secrets committed" exists to prevent. Only the .example is tracked.
config/wazuh_indexer/internal_users.yml
# Holds the wazuh-wui API password in PLAINTEXT. Only the .example is tracked.
config/wazuh_dashboard/wazuh.yml
# Agent enrollment password, plaintext. Only the .example is tracked.
wazuh/authd.pass

# Generated triage + digest artifacts (the .example templates ARE tracked)
triage/*_baseline.md
triage/*_delta.md
digest/*-digest.md
digest/*-intake.json
!digest/example-digest.md

# macOS
.DS_Store
